#  Animal Management System (Java OOP Project)

##  Project Overview

This project is a simple Java program that shows how inheritance works in Object-Oriented Programming (OOP). It uses animals to demonstrate how one class can get features from another class.

The system is built in a simple way to help understand how classes are connected.

---

## Project Structure (Model Design)
Animal (Main Class)
├── Dog
│ └── Puppy
└── Cat

Tiger (Final Class - separate)  
---

##  Classes Explanation

### Animal (Parent Class)
- Main class
- Contains basic information like name
- Other classes get features from this class

---

### Dog (Child Class)
- Inherits from Animal
- Has its own behavior (barks)

---

### Puppy (Child of Dog)
- Inherits from Dog
- Shows multilevel inheritance

---

### Cat (Child of Animal)
- Another child class
- Has its own behavior (meows)

---

### Tiger (Final Class)
- Special class
- Cannot be inherited by other classes

---

##  What This Project Shows

- How classes are connected (inheritance)
- How child classes reuse parent class code
- How methods can be changed in child classes
- How Java restricts multiple inheritance
- Use of simple OOP ideas

---

## ⚙️ Concepts Used

- Inheritance (extends)
- Method Overriding
- this keyword
- super keyword
- Constructor chaining
- Final class
- Protected access modifier
- Static method behavior

